#heading(numbering: none)[ABOUT THIS EDITION]

Only after I had read, and re-read, every page, table, and formula in this book, and transferred them from a long-lost but suddenly found `thedefiantred final4.doc`, could I appreciate the enormity of its contents. My youthful hubris when I wrote "This book describes all possibilities known to man on how to create red coloured glazes for ceramic application" on the website doesn't even do it justice.

It _does_ contain all possibilities known to man on how to create red coloured glazes for ceramic application.

Not only that, but its science was, and is, rock solid. Yes, the newly added chapter with corrections is over two pages, but it's mostly grammar and the fallout of busywork related to the rigid confines of computer code.

This electronic edition fills the need of many a would-be customer who contacted me over the years. I hope the knowledge of my late father continues to educate and inspire ceramists all over the world.

